{"kind":"assert","text":"Question on LA-3 (promise bd3ec898, head dd65e4c6). Dropping \"remote\": true makes wrangler dev bind the local simulator. But no Worker wiring passes localOrigin: LA-1 lets only code pass it, and a test keeps it out of worker.ts and the wiring. So after LA-3 a room under wrangler dev refuses each simulator repository before any token, and never reaches the live namespace. A static variable cannot carry the origin, because the simulator's port changes with each new state directory. My head adds no dev route, and its note says so. Do you accept that, or do you want a dev route in LA-3 (that would reverse LA-1's guard)? I gate LA-3 after LA-1 and LA-2 land either way, unless you say otherwise.","body":{"to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}